# Atlas Creed — example environment configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in real values. NEVER commit `.env.local`.
# `.gitignore` excludes every env file except this example.
#
# RULE (Build Plan §14): NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables are inlined into the client
# bundle at build time and are therefore PUBLIC, permanently, to anyone who
# opens devtools. No secret may ever carry that prefix. A test enforces this
# (tests/arch/env-boundary.test.ts).

# ─── Server-only ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required at runtime and server-only. Validated lazily by lib/env/server.ts.
# The production build itself needs none of these values. None may use a
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* name. See docs/operations/VERCEL_DEPLOYMENT.md for scope rules.

DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-example-pooler.us-east-2.aws.neon.tech/DATABASE?sslmode=require&channel_binding=require
# Must match the deployment scope that owns DATABASE_URL. Vercel Preview must
# use a Neon preview branch and the value `preview`; Production uses
# `production`. A mismatch fails closed at startup.
DATABASE_ENVIRONMENT=development

# Generate with `openssl rand -base64 32`. Never reuse the example value.
AUTH_SECRET=replace-with-at-least-32-random-characters
# Resend API key and a sender on a domain verified in Resend.
AUTH_RESEND_KEY=re_replace_me
AUTH_EMAIL_FROM=Atlas Creed <atlas@example.com>
# The one exact address permitted to request and redeem a magic link.
OWNER_EMAIL=owner@example.com
# Usually omit with Auth.js v5, including on Vercel. Only set for a deliberately
# nonstandard auth base path; production values must be HTTPS.
# AUTH_URL=

# OpenAI remains server-only. CI uses a fake AtlasModel and never requires a
# paid provider call.
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-replace-with-a-real-server-only-key
# Development/CI override only. Omit in Vercel Production; production preflight
# accepts only the official OpenAI API origin if this is explicitly set.
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4010/v1
ATLAS_CONVERSATION_MODEL=gpt-5.6-sol
ATLAS_BACKGROUND_MODEL=gpt-5.6-terra

# Application guardrails, distinct from the OpenAI account billing limit.
ATLAS_DAILY_SOFT_LIMIT_USD=10
ATLAS_MONTHLY_HARD_LIMIT_USD=150

# ─── Client-exposed (PUBLIC) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Atlas has no client-exposed environment variables. The product name is a
# source constant, not deployment configuration.
#
# Platform-owned (do not set in Vercel): NODE_ENV, VERCEL_ENV.
